From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: let a driver take frames redirected over XDP

An Ethernet frame another device redirects to an AP interface over XDP
needs nothing from mac80211 when the driver does the encapsulation. Add
ndo_xdp_xmit to the data interfaces, passing such frames to a new
xdp_xmit driver op, and a zero_touch debugfs switch per AP interface.
zero_touch asks the driver for Ethernet encapsulation and advertises the
interface as an XDP redirect target. The frames skip the TXQs, so
fq_codel, AQL and airtime fairness do not apply to them.

Export what the driver needs to send such a frame as mac80211 would: the
TID for its DSCP after the QoS map, admission control and reserved TIDs,
and a way to count it in the station's TX statistics. The DSCP part of
cfg80211_classify8021d() moves into cfg80211_classify_dscp() so that it
can be applied to a frame without an skb.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
